level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le18ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Tense and Past Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that   was happening at a time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular. <br>Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>.<br> Irregular verbs change in different ways.<br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did </span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask \u2026 ?</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">Did </span>is the past form of to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For Past Continuous, we add was/were + verb\u201cing\u201d to verbs.<br> Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201cing\u201d."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" look \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"looked \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were looking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" sit \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sat \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were sitting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\"